  "_about": "A pumped two-zone default room exactly as upstream 2.25.1 (80a7de8, the last HA-Irrigation-Strategy release before Jev became upstream) saved it: recorded by running that commit's own wizard in a real Home Assistant 2026.9.3, not written by hand. Pump + main line + two valves with the declared plumbing 'pump_mainline_valves', two probes on zone 1, a uS/cm EC probe on zone 2, feed EC/pH mapped, lights 6-18. Config entry version 1.1 (2.25.1 had no migration). 'operator_tuned_numbers' are values then set on the dashboard, with the attributes 2.25.1 stored beside them. 'registry' is every entity id 2.25.1 registered for this entry, keyed to its unique-id suffix. 'addon_options' is /data/options.json as Supervisor writes it from 2.25.1's config.yaml defaults (no Jev, sump or TypeSafe keys). 'controller_saved' is the /data/state.json controller 2.25.1 wrote after adopting the room and three shots plus one loop (its own _save_state).",
